# Temporary Debug Artifact Cleanup Rules

## Purpose

Agents often create one-off discovery scripts, debug runners, and JSON dumps while exploring UI flows, healing tests, or pinning locators.

These files are **not** project deliverables.

They must be removed before the task is marked complete.

Permanent learnings belong in specs, Page Objects, rules, skills, or approved scripts — not in scratch files left in the repository.

---

## Core Principle

**Discover and debug in temporary artifacts.**

**Deliver in approved project layers.**

**Delete temporary artifacts before finishing.**

Do not leave investigation output for the user to clean up unless the user explicitly asked to keep it.

---

## What Counts As Temporary Debug Artifacts

Remove after implementation, healing, or discovery when no longer needed:

- one-off Node scripts such as `scripts/debug-*.mjs`, `scripts/discover-*.mjs`, `scripts/scratch-*.mjs`;
- discovery output dumps such as `discover-*-output.json`, `*-discovery.json`, `*-debug-output.json` at repo root or elsewhere;
- ad-hoc investigation scripts outside approved project scripts;
- local scratch specs created only to probe locators or routes;
- copied MCP page YAML/JSON/log dumps saved into source folders (`.playwright-mcp/**` is already runtime output and must not be treated as source);
- temporary markdown notes at repo root created only for agent debugging;
- duplicate throwaway copies of Page Objects, specs, or plans created during experimentation.

---

## What Must Be Preserved

Do not delete as "cleanup":

- approved tests under `tests/**`;
- approved implementation under `src/test/**`;
- reviewed plans under `specs/**`;
- permanent framework scripts under `scripts/**` that are part of the starter (`check-conventions.mjs`, `project-cartographer.mjs`, and other documented maintenance scripts);
- intentional user-created files;
- files the user explicitly asked to keep for follow-up.

When unsure whether a script is permanent or temporary, classify as **unsure** and report it instead of deleting silently.

---

## When Cleanup Is Required

Cleanup is mandatory:

- after implementation verification passes or is documented;
- after healing/fix iteration completes;
- after UI discovery when temporary scripts or dumps were created;
- before reporting "done", "complete", or equivalent;
- before suggesting commit or PR, even if the user did not ask for cleanup.

If verification failed and more debugging is still in progress, cleanup happens at the **end of the task**, not after every failed attempt.

If the user explicitly asks to keep debug artifacts, keep only those named files and still remove unrelated temporary files from the same session.

---

## Required Workflow Step

Extend the default agent cycle with an explicit cleanup step:

```text
plan -> implement -> verify -> cleanup temporary debug artifacts -> report
```

For healing:

```text
diagnose -> fix -> verify -> cleanup temporary debug artifacts -> report
```

Cleanup is not optional hardening.

It is part of task completion.

---

## How To Clean Up

1. Inventory files created or modified during discovery/debug in the current task.
2. Classify each as **keep**, **remove**, or **unsure**.
3. Delete all **remove** files.
4. Transfer any still-useful findings into the proper layer before deletion:
   - locators and routes -> Page Objects / Components;
   - scenario decisions -> `specs/<feature>/<feature>.md` or `specs/e2e/<area>/<journey>.md`;
   - reusable commands -> approved scripts only when justified.
5. Report removed files in the final summary.

Do not move temporary debug scripts into `src/test/**` or `tests/**` to avoid deleting them.

---

## Secrets And Sensitive Output

Temporary debug files must not be committed.

Before deletion, ensure debug dumps did not capture:

- passwords;
- tokens;
- cookies;
- `.env` contents;
- real user credentials.

If sensitive data was written to a debug file, delete the file and do not summarize secret values in the report.

Prefer updating `.gitignore` patterns when a temporary artifact pattern is likely to recur.

Recommended ignore patterns:

```text
discover-*-output.json
scripts/debug-*.mjs
scripts/discover-*.mjs
scripts/scratch-*.mjs
```

---

## Reporting Requirements

Final task report must include a short **Cleanup** section when any temporary artifacts were created:

```text
Cleanup:
- removed: ...
- preserved: ...
- unsure (left untouched): ...
```

If no temporary artifacts were created, omit the section.

Do not claim implementation is complete while temporary debug files remain unless the user explicitly requested keeping them.

---

## Anti-Patterns

Avoid:

- leaving `discover-*-output.json` in the repo root;
- keeping a folder of `scripts/debug-*.mjs` after locators are pinned;
- treating MCP/runtime folders as deliverables;
- committing investigation JSON with generated credentials;
- converting one-off debug scripts into "just in case" permanent scripts without reuse evidence;
- deleting approved framework scripts during cleanup;
- deleting user-owned files without classification;
- skipping cleanup because verification passed.

---

## Main Principle

Temporary files help the agent investigate.

They are not part of the automation kit deliverable.

Clean them up before finishing.
